  <section aria-labelledby="minimal-about">
    <h2 id="minimal-about">About</h2>
    <p>Hi, I’m Lee. I live in Atlanta, by way of the DC area. I’m interested in how people work together and solve problems.</p>
    <p>I started out in biology and ecology, then moved into public health and population ethics. I’m a generalist by specialty and a social scientist by training. I do research, strategy and design work through <span class="goodneighbor-mark">goodneighbor, llc</span>.</p>
    <p>For useful references and rabbit holes, see <a href="/shelf/">Stacks</a>. Updated irregularly.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="minimal-worked-on">
    <h2 id="minimal-worked-on">Some things I’ve worked on or contributed to</h2>
    <ul class="minimal-clean-list minimal-clean-work">
      <li><strong>Community engagement and participatory design</strong><span>I led research with community members and program staff in Haiti to improve treatment-campaign design.</span><span>I contributed communication guidance to <a href="https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/9789240114944" rel="noreferrer">WHO’s toolkit on reaching people missed by treatment campaigns</a>.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Program design and organizational learning</strong><span>I developed <a href="https://www.cartercenter.org/resources/pdfs/news/health_publications/hispaniola/2022-carter-center-hispaniola-initiative-proceedings-summary.pdf#page=24" rel="noreferrer" aria-label="Decision tools — Carter Center program review (PDF)">decision tools</a> for campaign planning and worked with UNICEF colleagues on a <a href="https://campaigneffectiveness.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Collaborative-Action-Strategy-for-HCE-December2023.pdf#page=19" rel="noreferrer" aria-label="Evaluation framework — Health Campaign Effectiveness strategy (PDF)">framework for evaluating health campaigns</a>. I also coauthored <a href="https://journals.plos.org/plosntds/article?id=10.1371/journal.pntd.0008318" rel="noreferrer">research on campaign delivery in Haiti</a>.</span></li>
      <li>
        <strong>Product design</strong>
        <span>I contributed to product design for <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.eudecido.app&amp;hl=en_US" rel="noreferrer">EU DECIDO</a> for safety planning and support for women experiencing abuse in Brazil.</span>
        <span>I also contributed to <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.healthlink.women&amp;hl=en_US" rel="noreferrer">WoW: World of Women</a> for multilingual health education for women and families.</span>
      </li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://mesamalaria.org/resource-hub/gene-drive-technologies-for-malaria-control-in-africa-who-should-call-the-shots/" rel="noreferrer">Brokered Dialogue</a></strong><span>I co-produced a filmed dialogue about who should govern gene-drive technologies for malaria control in Africa. My work included interviewing, qualitative analysis, and coordinating remote production.</span></li>
    </ul>
